Created: May 10, 2022

[i]Last Updated May 6, 2026:[/i] Here are answers to frequently asked questions about my first game, [b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b]!

[h1]What is [i]Autopanic[/i]?[/h1]

[b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] is a fully diegetic twin-stick shooter with rogue-like elements in which you need to follow the guidance of an AI to reach the top floor of a mysterious facility. 

[b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] is intentionally designed to be a freeing experience where the player can learn the world at their own pace. I aim to deliver a game with some interesting narrative design along with satisfying fast-paced combat.

[h1]Where can I get [i]Autopanic[/i]?[/h1]

[b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] will soon be available on:

[list]
[*][url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/1274830]Steam[/url]
[/list]

[h1]What are the PC versions' minimum system requirements?[/h1]

[b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] is designed around Steam Deck's capability, targeting 800p/90FPS, which means as long as you have a rig faster than Steam Deck you should be able to run the game just fine.

[h1]Does [i]Autopanic[/i] have PC controller support?[/h1]

Yes! The game automatically work with any controller thrown at it. If not? That’s probably Unity’s fault. You can also toggle on/off Steam Input, both of which might lead to a proper detection of controller input.

[h1]What languages does the game support?[/h1]

[b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] features English and Traditional Chinese interface/subtitle, more language support is planned but will definitely take some time because I hope all languages to be written natively instead of being a plain translation.

[h1]Does [i]Autopanic[/i] support PC cloud saves?[/h1]

Yes! [b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] supports cloud saves on Steam. You may also find local copies of your saves under:
[list]
[*]Windows - [code]Documents\Saved Games\Autopanic[/code].
[*]macOS - [code]/Users/[UserName]/Library/Application Support/ChosenConcept/Autopanic/Save/save.dat[/code]
[/list]

[h1]You said there are Rogue-like elements?[/h1]

Each attempt will feature a different layout, enemy composition, and whatever rewards you can find.

I wouldn’t dare say this is a full-blown Rogue-like but there should be enough stuff around for you to enjoy!

[h1]Who are you, again...?[/h1]

I’m DK Liao, a developer from Taiwan!

I studied Chemical Engineering and Information Management. I’m extremely interested in Operation Research and Theory of Computation. And I’ve worked as video editor and translator at Ubisoft’s local branch for around six years.

I figure with all the things I’ve learnt, game development is the only choice to make them all shine! So here I am!

[h1]How long was [i]Autopanic[/i] in development?[/h1]

The first prototype of Autopanic is finished in April 2020. The actual development started at May 1st 2020. The project was put on hold several times. If you're interested, I've keep tabs on my development for the most part [url=https://blog.chosenconcept.dev/tags/autopanic/]here[/url] on this little site of mine.

[h1]Is [i]Autopanic[/i] a multiplayer game, or are there any plans for multiplayer?[/h1]

[b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] is a single-player game. I initially had some ideas for a couch coop mode, but that ended up being scrapped, for now. The gameplay and narrative of [b][i]Autopanic[/i][/b] has always been designed with a solo experience in mind anyways.

[h1]Does [i]Autopanic[/i] include DRM of any kind?[/h1]

Nope, you can copy the folder anywhere and it should still work!

[h1]I have more questions![/h1]

